.TH KIRO-YAY-AUR-CHECK 8 "2026-11-26" "Kiro" "Kiro System Tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-yay-aur-check \- switch the AUR check before yay builds on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-yay-aur-check
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-enable\fR | \fB\-\-disable\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR]
[\fB\-\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-yay-aur-check
manages one line in the user's
.IR ~/.config/yay/init.lua :
.PP
.EX
-- Kiro: AUR check \(em shows risky PKGBUILD lines before yay builds (kiro-aur-check)
if io.open("/usr/share/kiro/yay/aur-check.lua") then dofile("/usr/share/kiro/yay/aur-check.lua") end
.EE
.PP
That file registers yay's
.B AURPreInstall
hook (yay 13 or newer). yay runs it once per AUR package base, dependencies included,
before its menus, source downloads and builds; it runs
.BR kiro-aur-check (8),
and a non-zero exit stops yay.
.PP
yay has no system-wide config, so the check is switched on per user: new accounts get the
line from
.IR /etc/skel ,
existing ones through ATT or this command. The rest of init.lua is left alone, and the
line does nothing when kiro-system-files is removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-enable
Switch the check on; creates init.lua (and its folder) when there is none.
.TP
.B \-\-disable
Switch it off: the line is commented out, the marker stays.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print on, off or no-file. This is the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Another init.lua, for example a user's when run as root.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/yay/init.lua
yay's Lua config.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kiro/yay/aur-check.lua
The hook it loads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kiro-aur-check (8),
.BR kiro-paru-aur-check (8),
.BR yay (8)
